          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "The methodology meta-feature allows an analyst to describe the general class of activity, for example: spear-phish email, content-delivery attack, syn flood, port scan, etc. As with other feature types, this also allows more than one definition as necessary. For instance, a malicious spear-phishing email with malware attached may be categorized as both a \"spear-phish email\" and a \"content-delivery attack\"."
          }
        ]
      },
